        {
          "figmaNodeId": "90:31",
          "name": "Pricing FAQ",
          "widthPx": 175,
          "records": [
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:31",
              "name": null,
              "cells": [
                "Pricing FAQ"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "figmaNodeId": "90:32",
          "name": "grid",
          "widthPx": 1392,
          "records": [
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:33",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Is there really a free plan?",
                "Yes — the Free plan gives you one site, with the Besigner builder, forms, and media included. No credit card required."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:36",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Monthly or annual billing?",
                "Both. Annual is billed once up front and saves up to ~35% versus paying monthly. Switch anytime from the console."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:39",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "What happens if I exceed a plan limit?",
                "You’re not cut off. Extra sites, seats, datasets, storage, and API calls are metered at the rates in the usage table and itemized on your invoice."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:42",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "How do transaction fees work?",
                "Payments run on Stripe. Aglyn adds a transaction fee on top of Stripe’s processing — 0–5% depending on plan and digital vs. physical goods. It steps down as you move up — 1% on Scale, 0% from Advanced up."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:45",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Can I self-host instead of subscribing?",
                "Yes. Aglyn is Apache-2.0 — run it yourself with Docker and your own Firebase project (see the self-hosting guide), or use the hosted platform and skip the ops."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "90:48",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Can I change or cancel anytime?",
                "Upgrade, downgrade, or cancel whenever you like from the billing page. Plan changes prorate automatically."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "604:1272",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Have a promo code?",
                "Apply it at checkout — promotion codes work on any paid plan and show up itemized on your invoice."
              ]
            },
            {
              "figmaNodeId": "604:1275",
              "name": "qa",
              "cells": [
                "Do you offer SSO or an SLA?",
                "Both are coming for Enterprise contracts: SAML / OIDC single sign-on, an uptime SLA with a public status page, and priority support. Contact sales to plan around them."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "notes": null
    },
